  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m focused on establishing the core functionality for \"PulseLive,\" a Slido/Mentimeter alternative. I\'m prioritizing the essential features: poll/Q&A creation, QR code-based audience access (no login required!), and real-time result display. I\'m leaning toward a full-stack architecture with Express and Vite.\n\n\n**Evaluating Firebase Feasibility**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the feasibility of integrating Firebase. The need for real-time updates for poll results makes Firebase Firestore very attractive, given its `onSnapshot` listener. I\'m weighing whether a Firebase-only web application will suffice, or if the user\'s request for a full-stack app necessitates a custom Express server with techniques like long polling or SSE.\n\n\n**Assessing Dependency Readiness**\n\nI\'ve got the necessary dependencies installed and confirmed. Express is in, along with several UI libraries and Vite. I\'m especially interested in exploring SSE (Server-Sent Events) with an Express backend for the real-time functionality, which could be a robust alternative to Firebase for this project.\n\n\n**Analyzing Persistence Needs**\n\nI\'m now wrestling with persistence. I was considering Firebase for data durability, but I\'m questioning its necessity. I\'m leaning toward a clean Express backend that could use in-memory storage, local files, or, if absolutely needed, integrate with Firebase. I\'m exploring the option of implementing SSE or API polling for real-time updates without the added complexity of Firebase setup. Express is ready, so I need to explore these architecture options further.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will read the `package.json` file to understand the existing setup, including the scripts and dependencies."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 124058264
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
