  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the API**\n\nI\'ve created `src/types.ts` and am now focused on the backend server, `server.ts`. I\'m pondering room organization and leaning toward an in-memory database using a Map or object within `server.ts`. The API design phase has begun.\n\n\n**Defining the API Endpoints**\n\nNow I am solidifying the endpoint definitions. I\'ve mapped out the routes, like `/api/rooms` and `/api/rooms/:id/polls/:pollId/vote`, and their functionalities. I\'m focusing on POST methods for creating and manipulating data, GET for retrieval, and DELETE where necessary. I\'ve designed what each endpoint\'s request body will be.\n\n\n**Adding Demo Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the demo room! I\'ve decided to include a pre-populated \"DEMO\" room to boost the user experience, providing immediate interaction without any setup. It\'s user-friendly, and a great way to showcase features. The plan is to seed this room with sample polls and example questions in Q&A, offering a seamless and intuitive onboarding.\n\n\n**Addressing Robustness Concerns**\n\nNow, I\'m diving deeper into backend robustness. I\'m focusing on `server.ts` to integrate the Express API with Vite\'s development and production setups. The template in `Framework` -> `Full-Stack Applications (Express + Vite)` is helping with the structure. I\'m confirming that `express.json()` is the correct body parser. I\'m working to write the room generator. I\'m making sure to store the rooms in a `Map`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create the backend `server.ts` file, implementing the Express server with in-memory persistence, room management APIs, poll/Q&A handling, and Vite\'s dev/production middleware integration. This includes a pre-seeded demo room `\"DEMO\"` for immediate, zero-friction exploration."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 445804074
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
