  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering App.tsx Role**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on `/src/App.tsx`. My current thought is that it must handle routing and application state. I\'m planning to implement a check for URL hash changes and the initial URL hash when the component mounts. The hash change or mount logic will control the route and the state. I\'m now considering the approach.\n\n\n**Refining Hash-Based Routing**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement a simple, hash-based routing parser within `App.tsx`. I will leverage `window.location.hash` and manage `currentView` (landing, participant, presenter, projector) and `roomId`. This ensures clean, standard routing with bookmarking, sharing, and reliable new tab behavior. Empty hash or \"#/\" routes to landing. \"`/room/:id`\" will load the participant view, and other URL patterns will load other views.\n\nI will also implement state management for the currently loaded room, loading status, syncing status, and any error that might occur. This will rely on methods that will interface with the API. The methods are for creating and joining rooms.\n\n\n**Implementing API Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the API interactions for managing room state. I\'ll include logic to validate the room\'s existence and then update the URL hash to the appropriate room path. I\'ve begun integrating the various API methods to handle voting, asking questions, and presenter operations. Now, I\'m focusing on incorporating a polling interval to keep the local state synchronized with the server for active rooms. I\'m also ensuring the interval is handled correctly upon component unmount or room changes, and added state to show if syncing.\n\n\n**Refining Loading State**\n\nOkay, I\'ve decided to implement background state fetches. It will provide a seamless real-time experience! I\'ll ensure I don\'t show a full blocking spinner, maintaining a smooth user experience. I\'m now making sure that landing on an invalid room code will display a helpful message on the landing page, and also reset the hash to `#/`. Now, let\'s write `/src/App.tsx`. I should view the whole file before writing it.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will implement the central React routing and state coordination inside `src/App.tsx`. It manages real-time polling intervals (every 2 seconds) to keep presenter dashboards, projectors, and audience members perfectly in sync. It handles deep links using hash-based routing (`#/room/:id`, `#/room/:id/presenter`, etc.) which work inside iframe sandbox previews and across mobile browsers."
