  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Validating Application Files**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started by validating the application files. Specifically, I\'ve checked `/src/types.ts`, where the data models for `Poll`, `Question`, and `Room` are defined. After that, I validated `/src/lib/api.ts`, which contains helper functions to perform GET and POST requests, including `getOrCreateUserId` using `localStorage` for user identification.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Components**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the UI components, focusing on `/src/components/LandingPage.tsx`, which seems very user-friendly with its tabs for \"Join Session\" and \"Create Session\" and a live features explanation. I also like how the \"DEMO\" room is a quick-launch. The participant view in `/src/components/ParticipantView.tsx` is mobile-friendly, offers Q&A upvoting, and shows live polls. The presenter control and projector view round out the feature set nicely.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have designed and implemented **PulseLive**, a lightweight, real-time Slido and Mentimeter alternative. The app is fully full-stack, responsive, and ready to use, featuring real-time client-server synchronization, instant polls, interactive Q&A boards, and a high-impact projector interface with dynamic QR codes.\n\n### Architectural Overview\n\n1. **Robust Express Backend (`server.ts`)**:\n   - Manages rooms, polls, and Q&A queues in-memory with validation guards.\n   - Bootstraps with a pre-seeded `\"DEMO\"` room containing pre-populated, interactive polls and questions to allow immediate, zero-friction testing.\n   - Integrates Vite development middleware and compiles to a single, self-contained, high-performance production server via `esbuild`.\n\n2. **Unified Data Models (`src/types.ts` & `src/lib/api.ts`)**:\n   - Defines strict TypeScript interfaces for rooms, multi-choice polls, and upvoted questions.\n   - Implements automated client-side identification (`localStorage`) to secure voter integrity and prevent duplicate submissions or upvotes.\n\n3. **Elegant Visual Aesthetics & Fluid Transitions**:\n   - Styled with a modern, high-contrast light theme using the **Inter** font family for general user interfaces and **JetBrains Mono** for alphanumeric codes and live indicators.\n   - Utilizes fluid, staggered entering transitions powered by Framer Motion.\n\n---\n\n### Key Application Workspaces\n\n- **Premium Landing Page**: \n  - Allows presenters to create customized sessions and participants to join instantly using a 5-letter uppercase room code. \n  - Features a single-click quick launcher to enter the fully interactive live sandbox room.\n\n- **Mobile Audience Client (Participant View)**: \n  - Dual-tab layout for responding to polls and participating in the Q&A queue. \n  - Features real-time state listeners that display live multi-choice visual charts once a vote is cast, or sleek \"Waiting for Poll\" animated indicators. \n  - Includes a character-limited Q&A text field and a real-time sorted upvote board.\n\n- **Presenter Control Dashboard**: \n  - Provides dual-column moderation. \n  - Left Workspace: Create custom polls with dynamic, multi-choice option fields (up to 8 choices), activate drafts, close voting, or erase results.\n  - Right Workspace: Sort and moderate incoming audience questions. Presenters can delete, archive (hide from audience), or check off questions as answered live.\n\n- **Fullscreen Projector View**: \n  - A beautiful display designed to be projected onto a main stage wall. \n  - Integrates a responsive visualizer displaying large-format glowing horizontal bars for poll results.\n  - Features a dynamic, vector-rendered QR code that lets audience members scan and join instantly, without needing logins, credentials, or app downloads.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 297377999
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
